{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Bounded self-cleaning live-Jira-Cloud coordinator lifecycle lane + search-index-lag hardening\n\n## Problem\nThe epic's Live-External AC requires the RP-03 create-coordinator's create / binding-lifecycle /\ncommit-unknown / fuse exercised against **live Jira Cloud**. The only Cloud lane today is read-only AND\ngated off (`vars.AWS_S3_REHEARSAL_ROLE_ARN` unset) — SKIPPED even in green runs — so **no run has exercised\nlive-Cloud mutation**. Separately, `bridge check-access`'s `STEP_JQL_SEARCH` flakes on live REB: its wait\nis a FIXED 6x5s (no backoff), shorter than Jira Cloud's Lucene-index lag — the write lands (the by-key read\nright after passes), only SEARCH visibility lags.\n\n## §1 — Harden the search-index wait (`access_check.py`)\nReplace the fixed 6x5s loop with an env-tunable exponential-backoff budget:\n- `JIRA_PROBE_JQL_RETRIES` (default 10; was 6), `JIRA_PROBE_JQL_SLEEP` base (default 3; was 5),\n  `JIRA_PROBE_JQL_SLEEP_MAX` cap (default 30).- Sleep before retry k (k over 0..RETRIES-2) is `min(base*2**k, cap)` → defaults `[3,6,12,24,30,30,30,30,30]`\n  = 195s worst case (old ~25s budget timed out). Follows the capped-exponential shape used by the acli retry\n  floor (`_errors.MAX_BACKOFF_S`) but as a positive-result visibility poll. The `sleep_fn` seam is kept\n  (unit-testable without real sleeping); this poll helper is reused by §2's commit-unknown wait.\n\n## §2 — Live-Cloud coordinator lifecycle module (bounded, self-cleaning)\nNEW `tests/external/live_jira_cloud_mutation/test_cloud_coordinator_lifecycle.py` (+ `conftest.py`). Against\nlive REB it drives the epic's CREATE route `coordinate_full_create` (create_route.py:171) — composing\n`coordinate_create` (create_coordinator.py:235; create+commit-unknown) with `contain_created`\n(label/property/confirm binding) — for a plan of EXACTLY ONE throwaway ticket, then exercises the fuse via a\nbounded follow-up mutation (below):\n- **Write-bounding (shared-prod safety).** No full `bridge sync`; no legacy-route `--filter-local-ids`\n  (request.py:95 rejects it here). It acts only on the ONE plan handed to it (one create per plan) — NO\n  enumeration, NO write-back — so the only Jira mutations possible are the throwaway issue's create, its\n  containment label/property, and its delete.\n- **create + binding-lifecycle.** `create_execute` issues the physical create via the live Cloud client;\n  `record_key`/`attach_label`/`set_property`/`confirm` bind+contain it; asserts a confirmed containment\n  (`dependents_released`) with `jira` channel + `jira-` local-id provenance.\n- **commit-unknown recovery.** A second call injects an AMBIGUOUS create signal (simulated timeout) so\n  `_resolve_ambiguous` (create_coordinator.py:211) re-observes ONCE and ADOPTS the existing issue instead of\n  duplicating. Its `observe` FIRST waits until the dedup label search reflects the created issue (reusing\n  §1's helper), so adoption is attributable to the dedup path, not lag.\n- **fuse.** After the create, a bounded NON-create mutation plan (one label/summary op on the bound\n  throwaway key) is driven through `batch_dispatch.coordinate_and_fuse([mutation_plan], execute=...)`\n  (batch_dispatch.py:314) — the correct fuse API (runs non-create `coordinator.coordinate` then folds\n  outcomes through `PassFuse`, pass_fuse.py:96). Asserts the returned `CutoverReport` (tallies +\n  fuse_decisions + degraded) reflects that op.\n- **teardown (always) + one label scheme.** ONE env label `${REBAR_PROBE_RUN_LABEL}` (workflow:\n  `rebar-id:cloudprobe-<github.run_id>`; local: `rebar-id:cloudprobe-<uuid>`) is STAMPED on the created\n  issue by `attach_label`. The module deletes the issue by key in a `finally` (mirrors\n  access_check.py:217-224), then sweeps any issue carrying THAT label — the value §3's sweep keys on, so\n  the two cannot diverge; scoped to this run, not the shared `rebar-id:` prefix.\n- Gated by `_live_jira_ready()` + `REBAR_RUN_EXTERNAL=1` + Cloud creds, enrolling in the all-skip canary\n  (`tests/external/conftest.py`) like the DC modules.\n## §3 — Workflow lane\nAdd `jira-cloud-mutation-probe` to `.github/workflows/external-integration.yml` (`workflow_dispatch` +\nweekly cron): export `REBAR_PROBE_RUN_LABEL=rebar-id:cloudprobe-${{ github.run_id }}` + REB Cloud env from\nsecrets, run `bridge check-access` (preflight) THEN the module, and on BOTH failure AND cancel run an\nalways-run teardown sweeping `${REBAR_PROBE_RUN_LABEL}` via acli (`acli jira workitem search --jql\n\"labels = ...\" --json` then `acli jira workitem delete --key <KEY> --yes` per hit; `--yes` REQUIRED per\nacli.py bug-3256 so the non-TTY sweep does not block on stdin). Same label the module stamps, scoping the\nsweep to the run.\n\n## §4 — Workflow-structure unit test\n`tests/unit/test_external_integration_cloud_mutation_workflow.py` (modelled on\n`test_jira_dc_capability_map_workflow.py`) proves the lane exists, exports `REBAR_PROBE_RUN_LABEL` from the\nrun id, runs check-access + the module, and has an always-run teardown with `--yes` keyed on that label.\n## §5 — Docs\nUpdate `tests/external/live_jira_cloud_s3/README.md`: the read-only rule is that suite's choice; the new\nlane is bounded, self-cleaning, prod-safe.\n\n## Prerequisites (operational)\nThe Cloud lane needs live REB Cloud credentials as repo config — `JIRA_URL` and `JIRA_USER` as repository\n**variables** and `JIRA_API_TOKEN` as a repository **secret** (the exact names the workflow's env block and\n`tests/external/live_jira_cloud_mutation/_cloud_mutation_support._CLOUD_CRED_VARS` consume). The operator\nprovisions/confirms them BEFORE the GREEN-run AC is evaluated. Missing creds cannot masquerade as success:\nthe module enrols in the all-skip canary, so a skipped Cloud lane FAILS.\n\n## Consumers to update (enumerated)\n- `tests/scripts/bridge/test_jira_capability_probe.py` (asserts `call_count == 6`, `delays == [5,5,5,5,5]`)\n  updated in the SAME change to the new 10-attempt `delays == [3,6,12,24,30,30,30,30,30]` plus an\n  env-override case recomputing from overridden base/cap/retries.\n\n## Surface-parity census\n- CLI (`bridge check-access`): in scope — JQL backoff exercised through it.\n- library (`run_access_check`; `coordinate_full_create`+`PassFuse`): in scope — unit tests drive the\n  backoff; the live module drives the create route + fuse.\n- automated caller (lane / live module): in scope — E2E oracle is the live run.\n- MCP/API: out of scope (no MCP tool). dual-direction: outbound create only in a one-plan call, no mirror.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] `access_check.py` JQL wait is env-tunable exponential backoff (defaults 10 / 3 / 30 → sleeps\n  `[3,6,12,24,30,...]`); `sleep_fn` seam preserved; write-landing still confirmed by the by-key read.\n  Evidenced by new unit tests asserting the schedule and env-override recomputation.\n- [x] `tests/scripts/bridge/test_jira_capability_probe.py` updated to the new schedule/defaults and passes.\n- [x] The live-Cloud module drives `coordinate_full_create` for ONE throwaway plan (create/binding +\n  commit-unknown-after-visibility-wait + fuse), asserts known_key is the throwaway key and no other, and\n  ALWAYS deletes (finally + `${REBAR_PROBE_RUN_LABEL}` sweep). Enrols in the all-skip canary.\n- [x] The `jira-cloud-mutation-probe` lane exports `REBAR_PROBE_RUN_LABEL`, runs check-access + module, and\n  has an always-run `acli jira workitem delete --key <KEY> --yes` teardown keyed on that label. Per §4.\n- [x] With Cloud secrets provisioned (see Prerequisites), a dispatched Live External Integration run shows\n  the new Cloud-mutation lane GREEN and the DC lane GREEN. Evidenced by the run URL commented on the epic.\n- [x] `tests/external/live_jira_cloud_s3/README.md` documents the read-only rule as suite-scoped and the\n  new bounded self-cleaning mutating lane.\n- [x] `make lint && make typecheck && make test` green.\n\n## Verify commands\n- `make test PYTEST_ARGS=\"tests/scripts/bridge/test_jira_capability_probe.py tests/unit/test_external_integration_cloud_mutation_workflow.py\"` and `make lint`\n\n## Portability\nCI-agnostic: backoff is library behavior; the lane surfaces an op-linked probe (check-access + a\npytest module) that runs locally with the same env — nothing gated on one CI system."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787896703982882001,"uuid":"083814b2-174b-4dab-ad4a-0490c45b5682"}